WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.680
Who is the wealthiest among Earth's Mightiest
Heroes?

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:07.000
The amount Disney pays the actors portraying
our favorite Marvel characters may surprise

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.500
you.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.880
Let's take a look at just how much the actors
who play the Avengers are actually worth offscreen.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:17.220
At a time when the superhero genre was thought
to be on its last legs, cinematically, Iron

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:22.269
Man opened huge and launched what would become
known as Phase One, the initial slate of movies

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:24.920
that set the baseline for the Marvel Cinematic
Universe.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.720
Robert Downey Jr. has appeared in multiple
MCU movies since as the eccentric billionaire

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.860
Tony Stark, aka Iron Man.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.660
He's not quite a billionaire himself, but
in Forbes magazine's list of highest paid

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.500
actors for 2018, Downey came in third, with
an income of $81 million.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.750
That includes an estimated $15 million upfront
for his supporting role in Spider-Man: Homecoming.

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.400
He earned several times that amount for Avengers:
Infinity War.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:55.540
It's rumored that Downey was paid $200 million
total for that film and its sequel, Avengers:

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.040
Endgame.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.800
That's a long way from the reported $50 million
he received for appearing in The Avengers,

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.240
and even further from the $2.5 million he
was paid for the original Iron Man.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:10.620
According to Chris Hemsworth, he totally blew
his first audition for Thor, only to see his

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.540
younger brother Liam get callback after callback
for the role.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:18.360
When it eventually became clear that Liam
wouldn't be cast, Chris tried again, recording

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:22.689
a second audition tape while on location filming
Cabin in the Woods with his future Avengers

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:23.840
director Joss Whedon.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.060
This time Chris nailed it, and claimed his
rightful title as God of Thunder.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.350
Forbes' list of highest-paid actors placed
Hemsworth fourth in 2018, with an income of

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:35.180
$64.5 million.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.320
That number includes his earnings from the
blockbusters Thor: Ragnarok and Avengers:

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:40.000
Infinity War.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.200
The original Thor, from Phase One, reportedly
paid the actor just $150,000.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.880
In 2018, Chris Evans finished filming his
tenth MCU outing as Captain America - Avengers:

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:52.400
Endgame.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.320
This entry in the Avengers series is slated
to be Evans’ final appearance in the MCU,

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:02.160
according to multiple reports that were kinda
sorta confirmed by a tweet from Evans himself.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.160
Evans tweeted,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.240
"Officially wrapped on Avengers 4.

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:07.920
Playing this role over the last 8 years has
been an honor.

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.870
To everyone in front of the camera, behind
the camera, and in the audience, thank you

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:12.870
for the memories.

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:13.820
Eternally grateful."

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.760
Evans leaves the role considerably wealthier
than he was when he started.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:24.330
He was paid $1 million for Captain America:
The First Avenger in 2011, but in 2018, Forbes

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.880
listed him as the 10th highest paid actor
in the world.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:32.180
He reportedly earned $34 million over the
preceding year, largely from portraying Steve

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.860
Rogers in Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.600
Thanks for your service, Cap!

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:41.220
Scarlett Johansson has appeared in multiple
Marvel films, but will finally get the largest

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.580
payday of her career with her leading role
in the upcoming Black Widow standalone movie.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:50.860
Johansson is reportedly set to make $15 million
for her appearance, reportedly matching what

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:54.260
Chris Hemsworth and Chris Evans received for
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:59.090
The film is said to be set before the events
of the Avengers films, and will follow a chapter

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.820
of the character's journey from Russian spy
to superhero.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.340
Johansson received a "low seven-figure" salary
for her work in the first Avengers movie,

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:09.880
after making her MCU debut in Iron Man 2 in
2012.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:15.940
Black Widow doesn't have a release date yet,
but is slated to begin filming in 2019 - a

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:19.819
start date that would seem poised to make
it the second female superhero-centered film

00:03:19.819 --> 00:03:23.959
to be released by Marvel following Captain
Marvel, starring Brie Larson, which is set

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:26.099
to be released March 8, 2019.

00:03:27.209 --> 00:03:32.689
Brie Larson was cast as Captain Marvel fresh
off her Best Actress Oscar for 2015's Room.

00:03:32.689 --> 00:03:37.410
Needless to say, a star of her caliber brings
not only a well-known name, but an expectation

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.480
of on-screen depth to the MCU.

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.960
Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige, speaking
to Vanity Fair, said of the casting,

00:03:43.969 --> 00:03:48.790
"Captain Marvel has powers that far surpass
many of her heroic counterparts, and in order

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.230
to bring this superhero to life and make her
relatable and disarming we needed an actress

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.780
with both range and humanity."

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:59.480
Bringing her pedigree to the role of Captain
Marvel gave Larson some leverage at the negotiating

00:03:59.480 --> 00:03:59.980
table.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.000
She reportedly earned $5 million for the movie
- a large paycheck for an opening lead vehicle

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:05.880
in the MCU.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:10.499
It's also been reported that Larson's high-dollar
deal includes a seven-picture commitment that

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:13.580
locks her into multiple franchises for the
foreseeable future.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.060
The MCU has steadily added star power as it's
grown in scope - narratively as well as in

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.040
terms of box office - and Benedict Cumberbatch
offers a distinguished example.

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:27.760
During the exhaustive casting process for
Doctor Strange, Marvel looked at many actors

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:32.220
with similar levels of celebrity, ultimately
passing on Ethan Hawke, Joaquin Phoenix, and

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:32.780
Jared Leto.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.080
Before he landed the gig, Cumberbatch was
nominated for an Oscar for his role in The

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.980
Imitation Game and was quite well known for
his work on BBC's Sherlock.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:46.840
Cumberbatch was reportedly paid $3.2 million
for appearing in Doctor Strange, Thor: Ragnarok,

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.500
Avengers: Infinity War, and Avengers: Endgame.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.650
He's said to be making just under $10 million
for the upcoming Doctor Strange 2, which is

00:04:54.650 --> 00:04:56.780
scheduled to begin filming in 2019.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:02.560
In 2012, Bruce Banner finally became science
bros with Tony Stark in The Avengers.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:07.280
But Mark Ruffalo was in a very different position
entering the film, portraying a character

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:12.460
that had his own Phase One standalone - 2008's
The Incredible Hulk - without having actually

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:13.800
played the role himself.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:19.900
As a result, Ruffalo earned a rumored $2 million
for The Avengers, and $2.8 million for Avengers:

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:20.840
Age of Ultron.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.680
That salary increased for Avengers: Infinity
War to a rumored $5-to-6 million.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.900
The CGI Hulk is one of the most expensive
characters to bring to the screen, but Ruffalo

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:35.030
earns a relatively modest payday for playing
his human counterpart - at least compared

00:05:35.030 --> 00:05:36.060
to the other Avengers.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:40.820
Could a standalone Hulk film raise Ruffalo's
asking price to Robert Downey Jr.'s level?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.660
Not likely.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.400
According to Ruffalo himself, a solo Hulk
film isn't anywhere close to being a reality.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:52.620
Following a D23 Panel in 2017, Ruffalo commented
on the subject, putting the rumors to rest:

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:55.740
"A standalone Hulk movie will never happen.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:06:02.660
Because Universal has the rights to the standalone
Hulk movie and, for some reason, they don't

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:04.140
know how to play well with Marvel."

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:08.020
Ruffalo added that he only has "two or three
years" before he's too old to even play the

00:06:08.020 --> 00:06:08.520
Hulk.

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.680
Most of the Avengers signed contracts for
at least six movies.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.480
It's been said that Jeremy Renner's contract
covers six films, minimum, likely with a solo

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.640
movie in there somewhere.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.680
However, there is currently no Hawkeye or
Ronin standalone film in any stage of production.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:28.800
In fact, we haven't seen Renner in an MCU
film since Captain America: Civil War's cliffhanger

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:29.520
of an ending.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.940
Hawkeye may have been out of his league in
Infinity War's cosmic-level event, but his

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:36.240
no-show did not go unnoticed by fans.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:40.860
Kevin Feige said of the internet's interest
in the glaring absence of the linchpin Avenger,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:44.960
"[...] I love that people go from 'Oh, Hawkeye
is just lucky to be there' to 'Oh where is

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:45.460
he?

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:46.380
He's not there?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.060
What's going to happen?

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:47.860
We need Hawkeye.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:48.920
We want more Hawkeye.'"

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:54.039
For the first Avengers film, Renner was rumored
to have made at least $2 million, with a bump

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.560
up to a rumored $6 million for Age of Ultron.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.220
We can assume that after taking Infinity War
off, Renner is likely in line for another

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:05.420
pay raise in his hotly anticipated return
to the franchise in Avengers: Endgame.

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.220
And then there's that rumored Hawkeye TV show
potentially in-the-works for Disney's upcoming

00:07:10.230 --> 00:07:15.139
streaming service, Disney+, which could see
Renner-as-Barton training the next generation

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:19.160
of Avengers archer, and likely getting a nice
payday for his troubles.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:24.540
Not much is known about the details of Paul
Bettany's MCU contract, but he told Jimmy

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:28.240
Fallon in 2015 that his voice work alone was
quite profitable:

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:33.340
"I would work for about 40 minutes and then
they would give me a huge bag of cash.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.920
And then I would walk out like I was a thief."

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.680
He's also has joked about his jealousy of
Robert Downey Jr.'s compensation.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.420
Speaking to Hollywood Outbreak, the Vision
and Jarvis actor quipped,

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:47.900
"I like my character, but I'd love Robert
Downey Jr.'s profit participation."

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:53.520
Elizabeth Olsen made her MCU debut in a mid-credits
sequence at the end of Captain America: The

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:54.400
Winter Soldier.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.860
She's gone on to portray the Scarlet Witch
in three more films and is slated to appear

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.240
in Avengers: Endgame.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:04.599
Olsen has been tight-lipped about her contract
with Marvel, but she's made it known that

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.560
she doesn't concern herself with the details.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:09.240
Olsen told the Independent in 2016,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.360
"I let the people that I hire do my contracts.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:14.480
I would work for nothing and they know that."

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:19.260
Samuel L. Jackson has starred in dozens of
films during his prolific career.

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:24.180
In total, his movies have earned just over
$5.7 billion worldwide.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:29.000
According to Box Office Mojo, that makes Jackson
the highest-grossing actor of all time.

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.480
Jackson first appeared in the Marvel Cinematic
Universe as Nick Fury in a stinger at the

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.220
end of Iron Man in 2008.

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:39.960
When he initially signed on to play the role
of the Avengers' assembler, it was for nine

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:40.460
movies.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:45.500
Jackson is set to play a large, digitally
de-aged part in the upcoming Captain Marvel,

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.760
his ninth MCU film.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.200
Will he re-up with another contract?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.660
It seems likely, given that Fury is often
the connective tissue in the far-flung stories

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:57.060
of the MCU, but so far, no details have emerged.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.820
It's said that he received $4-to-6 million
for the first Avengers film, and his long-term

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:04.600
contract likely had built-in modest raises.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:09.040
With nine paydays under his belt, it remains
to be seen how many more are in Jackson's

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.260
future with the MCU.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.240
It should be noted that what an actor makes
for each film and the details of their contract

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:21.180
with a given studio are often at best unverified
rumors and at worst spurious speculation.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:26.080
They come from lightly sourced rumors in industry
trades and are often reported as gospel.

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:30.320
It's definitely in the studio's interest to
keep the truth under wraps to protect their

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:32.580
negotiation power as much as possible.

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:37.060
But we've heard the same stories repeatedly
about the way Marvel pays its stars - the

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:41.290
studio puts up a little collateral upfront,
banking on the fact that the intellectual

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:45.780
property will carry the box office and set
the stage for future large paydays.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:52.720
Examples include Tom Hiddleston, who reportedly
made $160,000 for Avengers, and Zoe Saldana,

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:58.280
whose base salary for Guardians of the Galaxy
is said to be about $100,000 before her profit

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:58.820
participation bonus.

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:03.260
Chadwick Boseman is said to have been paid
about $2 million for his starring role in

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:07.180
the billion-dollar Black Panther, with a well-deserved
raise said to be on the way.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:12.410
Chris Pratt was reported to have earned $1.5
million for playing Star-Lord in the original

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:16.140
Guardians, with a bump up to $5 million for
Avengers: Infinity War.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:21.700
Paul Rudd, another actor with a well-known
body of work, may have only received $300,000

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:26.190
for the first Ant-Man, but his total MCU compensation
is likely much, much higher.

